;; A bake-off, as a person types it - three lines. `bb bake-off new` asks for them at a terminal;
;; `bb bake-off run <plan>/bake-offs/<id>/bake-off.edn` expands them through the catalogue
;; (`bb models`) and `routes.edn` into full role blocks (written beside as resolved.edn), runs
;; every case with every candidate ONCE, has the judge read the answers blind and map where they
;; agree and disagree, and renders TABLE.md. The person marks each row real or not in marks.edn;
;; the per-dollar figures render from the marks, never from the judge.
;;
;;   :role        an act the roster lists: plan-reviewer, blueprint-reviewer, spec-reviewer
;;                (the dispatched roles come with the loop runner)
;;   :candidates  "<model slug or a word> <effort>" - "grok" resolves to the newest Grok; the
;;                effort is the family's highest when left out
;;   :judge       the same form; never a candidate, and another family when the field allows
;;   :cases       optional - paths; by default everything on disk for the act under the plan
;;   :parallel    optional - how many readings run at once (4 when left out); a reading is one
;;                completion with no tools, so the pool is bounded by the providers' patience. A
;;                record a stopped run already wrote is reused, so a run resumes rather than repeats;
;;                delete records/ to read everything again
;;
;; Copy this to <plan>/bake-offs/<id>/bake-off.edn and edit it.

{:role :blueprint-reviewer
 :candidates ["anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 high"
              "openai/gpt-5.6-sol high"
              "x-ai/grok-4.7 medium"]
 :judge "openai/gpt-6-astra high"}
